{
  "id": 239285639,
  "iid": 11522,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "packet-cql.c: deal with NULL and zero length map and set values",
  "description": "In the case where the byte length is -1 (NULL value), we need to ensure the metadata offset is progressing:\nskipping the (irrelevant) offset of the type fields.\nIn the case where the byte length is 0, we also need to ensure the offset progresses in a similar manner.\n\nThis fixes parsing of a RESULT message which has both cases in it and now it is being parsed correctly.\n\nSigned-off-by: Yaniv Kaul <yaniv.kaul@scylladb.com>",
